{"text": "JORRIS FICE\n120 PARK AVENUE, NEW YORK, N.Y. 10017-5592\n\nTo: Records Coordinators DATE\nPhilip Morris Companies Inc.\nPhilip Morris Incorporated\nPhilip Morris Management Corp.\n\nJune 28, 1995\n\nGLeezoL2oz\n\nFROM: William Lynch III\n\nRE: Records Disposal Suspension Notice\n\nAs Records Coordinators, it is your responsibility to see that all records are managed\npursuant to the Records Management Policy.\n\nRequests for certain records, ail or most of which are already subject to disposai\nsuspension under the applicable Philip Morris Records Management Manual, were recently\nserved in litigation pending against Philip Morris Incorporated. An order has been entered in\nthe same litigation requiring that certain records be.preserved.\n\nThis notice will serve to place the records described in the attachment to this\nmemorandum under disposal suspension, to the extent they are not already under suspension\nand extends to ail such records whatever their media. Except for electronic records which mus\nbe preserved in originai electronic form pursuant to previously issued disposal suspensior\nnotices dated April 6, 1994, April 21, 1994, May 4, 1994 and July 28, 1994, electronic mail and othe:\nelectronic records, if any, should be retained by printing and retaining a paper copy only, ir\naccordance with the usual retention practice for electronic records subject to each Records\nManagement Manual\u2019s Appendix entitled Topics Subject to Disposal Suspension. However\nelectronic records subject to disposal suspension that are incapable of being printed mus\ncontinue to be maintained in electronic form.\n\nRecords already subject to disposal suspension are listed in the Appendix entitled Topic.\nSubject to Disposal Suspension in the applicable Records Management Manual and in prio\nrecords disposal suspension notices. Prior disposal suspension notices and the Appendi>\n\nentitled Topics Subject to Disposal Suspension in the applicable Records Management Manua\nremain in effect without change. =\n\nIf there is any question about whether a record is subject to disposal suspension 0\nregarding the appropriate means or media for retention, the record should be retained in it\noriginal media pending review by the Legal Department.",
